BT /F1 10 Tf 50 720 Td (IN THE MADRAS HIGH COURT \(PRINCIPAL SEAT, CHENNAI\)
CASE NO: Crl.A. No. 512 of 2026
CNR NUMBER: MHC010912342026
YEAR: 2026

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Justice A.D. Jagadish Chandira

PARTIES:
M. Sivakumar
... Petitioner\(s\) / Appellant\(s\)
Versus
State represented by Inspector of Police, All Women Police Station, Tambaram
... Respondent\(s\)

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Protection of Children from Sexual Offences Act 2012, Juvenile Justice Act 2015

SECTIONS & PROVISIONS:
POCSO Act Section 4, POCSO Act Section 29, JJ Act Section 94

KEY TOPICS & ISSUES:
POCSO, Statutory Presumption, Rebuttal of Presumption, Age Determination, Ossification Test

================================================================================
                                   JUDGMENT
================================================================================

1. FACTS OF THE CASE:
Appellant convicted under POCSO. Victim age was determined solely on radiological ossification with 2-year margin of error.

2. ISSUES FRAMED:
How is statutory presumption under Section 29 POCSO Act to be balanced when age of victim is hovering on border of majority?

3. LEGAL RATIO & FINDINGS:
Presumption under Section 29 POCSO Act arises only after prosecution conclusively establishes victim's minority beyond reasonable doubt.

4. FINAL ORDER:
Criminal Appeal Allowed; Conviction under POCSO Act set aside; Age proof ossification test inconclusive.

Ordered and decreed accordingly.

Hon'ble Justice A.D. Jagadish Chandira
Madras High Court \(Principal Seat, Chennai\)
[LEXGUARD REPOSITORY CRYPTOGRAPHIC SEAL]
) Tj ET
